// hzip GUI executable resources.
//
// Resource ID MUST be 1.
//   * gpui's Windows backend loads the window-class icon with
//     LoadImageW(GetModuleHandleW(NULL), MAKEINTRESOURCE(1), IMAGE_ICON, ...)
//     (gpui-pre-windows, src/platform.rs `load_icon`). Without this resource the
//     titlebar, taskbar and Alt-Tab entry fall back to the generic system icon.
//   * Explorer's file-manager icon for the exe, and the shell-extension menu icon
//     (`{exe},0` -- written by hzip-platform::context_menu and returned by
//     hzip-shell's IExplorerCommand::GetIcon), resolve to the lowest-ID icon
//     group of this image, i.e. this entry.
//
// The .ico is generated from assets/logo/hzip-<N>.png by build/icons/make-icons.ps1;
// do not edit it by hand.
//
// NOTE: comments here are intentionally ASCII-only -- rc.exe is invoked without
// a codepage flag, so non-ASCII bytes would be parsed in the ANSI codepage.
1 ICON "assets/logo/hzip.ico"
